{"assets":["/statement-assets/6dd435984762d023393396c1515bea14e58333079bd9344bf724d7d13dea8360.png","/statement-assets/ae640d5fbb660d7e704a2b12a20158685a94eb3bb0e2e85ca70278dc14ddf6cd.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1817","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Toy Machine"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a toy machine with toys arranged in two rows of $$$n$$$ cells each ($$$n$$$ is odd)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6dd435984762d023393396c1515bea14e58333079bd9344bf724d7d13dea8360.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initial state for $$$n=9$$$."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially, $$$n-2$$$ toys are placed in the non-corner cells of the top row. The bottom row is initially empty, and its leftmost, rightmost, and central cells are blocked. There are $$$4$$$ buttons to control the toy machine: left, right, up, and down marked by the letters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" correspondingly."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When pressing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", all the toys will be moved simultaneously in the corresponding direction and will only stop if they push into another toy, the wall or a blocked cell. Your goal is to move the $$$k$$$-th toy into the leftmost cell of the top row. The toys are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n-2$$$ from left to right. Given $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$, find a solution that uses at most $$$1\\,000\\,000$$$ button presses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To test out the toy machine, a "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://assets.codeforces.com/files/56ff21637146a30d/game.html"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"web page"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" is available that lets you play the game in real time. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line contains two integers, $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$5 \\le n \\le 100\\,000$$$, $$$n$$$ is odd, $$$1 \\le k \\le n-2$$$) — the number of cells in a row, and the index of the toy that has to be moved to the leftmost cell of the top row."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On a single line, output a description of the button presses as a string of at most $$$1\\,000\\,000$$$ characters. The string should only contain the characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The $$$i$$$-th character in the string is the $$$i$$$-th button that is pressed. After all the button presses are performed, the $$$k$$$-th toy should be in the leftmost cell of the top row."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple solutions, print any. The number of button presses does not have to be minimized."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRDL\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRDL\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there will be $$$5-2 = 3$$$ toys. The first toy needs to end up in the leftmost cell of the top row. The moves "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RDL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will achieve this, see the picture for a better understanding. Another possible solution would be to do one button press "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ae640d5fbb660d7e704a2b12a20158685a94eb3bb0e2e85ca70278dc14ddf6cd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Visualization of the moves for the first example."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1817D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1817/problem/D"}